# Cloudflare Pages: every path renders the SPA.
#
# The router owns the URL space (/projects, /editor/<id>, /docs/<slug>, …), so a
# cold load of any of them must return index.html with a 200 rather than a 404.
# `200` here means REWRITE, not redirect — the address bar keeps the deep link.

# `/api/*` is the Node backend (server/), which does NOT run on Pages. Without
# this rule the SPA catch-all below answers those requests with index.html and a
# 200, so the client parses HTML as JSON and reports a bogus failure (the
# settings dialog showed "dev server not ready?" for exactly this). Answer them
# with an honest 404 + JSON instead, so callers can degrade cleanly.
# `/api/*` is handled by functions/api/[[path]].js (Pages supports only 3xx and
# 200 proxying here, not 404 rewrites), and `/auth/*` by functions/auth/.
/*  /index.html  200
